From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sheepsticked <72666364+Sheepsticked@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] report equipment errors with their text (AT+CMEE=2)

Upstream: https://github.com/wdoekes/asterisk-chan-dongle @ 31eb619600d5ce93237cd440c72db0bc33d7adfe
Purpose: with AT+CMEE=0 a refused command ends in a bare ERROR; with
         AT+CMEE=2 the modem names the reason (+CME ERROR: network
         rejected request), which AtDone then carries as its Error
         (applies on top of 0010)

The initialization asks for the text form. +CME ERROR is handled like
ERROR by every response handler, so nothing else changes.
---
 at_command.c | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/at_command.c b/at_command.c
index 319d81e..5f4ac68 100644
--- a/at_command.c
+++ b/at_command.c
@@ -134,9 +134,8 @@ EXPORT_DEF int at_enqueue_initialization(struct cpvt *cpvt, at_cmd_t from_comman
 		ATQ_CMD_DECLARE_ST(CMD_AT_CGMM, "AT+CGMM\r"),
 		/* Get software version */
 		ATQ_CMD_DECLARE_ST(CMD_AT_CGMR, "AT+CGMR\r"),
-		/* set MS Error Report to 'ERROR' only.
-		 * TODO: change to 1 or 2 and add support in response handlers */
-		ATQ_CMD_DECLARE_ST(CMD_AT_CMEE, "AT+CMEE=0\r"),
+		/* report equipment errors as +CME ERROR: <text> (handled like ERROR) */
+		ATQ_CMD_DECLARE_ST(CMD_AT_CMEE, "AT+CMEE=2\r"),
 
 		/* IMEI Read */
 		ATQ_CMD_DECLARE_ST(CMD_AT_CGSN, "AT+CGSN\r"),
